XSS / Local Exploits: If keys are stored in localStorage, a cross-site scripting attack can leak them.
MITM Key Substitution: A malicious server could return its own public keys instead of the receiver''s.'), 'C'),
  TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
WHERE EXISTS (
  SELECT 1 FROM "notes"."Note" n
  WHERE n.id = 'ae8da301-e12f-7b23-91e2-67ce7e137185' AND n.visibility = 'PUBLIC' AND n."publishedVersionId" = 'e66df435-bb43-76a5-89d4-5e35a0c62198' AND n."deletedAt" IS NULL
