SELECT 'e3f7c71e-04a6-741a-8554-00792976b6fc', 'a1ec6ff6-2ff3-7ea2-846a-00461a9c67f9', 'Event Driven Arch', 'Event Driven Arch', 'A design pattern where services communicate by producing and consuming events, enabling loose coupling and high scalability.
Definition
In event-driven architecture, services emit events when something happens (order placed, user signed up). Other services subscribe to relevant events and react. The event broker (Kafka, SNS) is the central nervous system.
Event Flow Example
User Places Order → order.created event → Kafka Topic → Inventory Service
spacer → spacer → spacer → Email Service
CQRS + Event Sourcing: Command Query Responsibility Segregation separates read and write models. Event Sourcing stores every state change as an event — the current state is derived by replaying events. Powerful but complex.',
  setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Event Driven Arch'), 'A')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Event Driven Arch'), 'B')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'A design pattern where services communicate by producing and consuming events, enabling loose coupling and high scalability.
Definition
In event-driven architecture, services emit events when something happens (order placed, user signed up). Other services subscribe to relevant events and react. The event broker (Kafka, SNS) is the central nervous system.
Event Flow Example
User Places Order → order.created event → Kafka Topic → Inventory Service
spacer → spacer → spacer → Email Service
CQRS + Event Sourcing: Command Query Responsibility Segregation separates read and write models. Event Sourcing stores every state change as an event — the current state is derived by replaying events. Powerful but complex.'), 'C'),
  TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
