SELECT '0224be9a-39c9-7f27-8cd1-25cf6f13bb99', 'dd97f4cf-3d28-7857-be3c-cae506b5a516', 'Instagram', 'Instagram', 'A photo/video sharing platform with 2B+ users. Core challenges: photo storage at scale, feed generation, follow graph.
Requirements
Functional
Upload photos/videos · Follow users · View feed of followed users · Like & comment · Stories (24h expiry)
Non-Functional
500M DAU · Read-heavy (100:1 read/write) · Photo uploads must be durable · Feed load <200ms · Eventual consistency OK for feed
Estimates
DAU: 500M
Photos uploaded / day: 100M
Avg photo size: 200 KB
Storage / day: 20 TB
10-year storage: 73 PB
Photo Upload Flow
Client → API Gateway → Upload Service → S3 / Object Store
x → x ↓ Message Queue → CDN Invalidation + Feed Update
Feed Generation: Push vs Pull
Fan-out on Write (Push)
When user posts, pre-populate feed for all followers. Feed reads are instant. But celebrity with 100M followers = 100M writes per post. Instagram uses hybrid — fan-out for regular users, pull for celebrities.
Fan-out on Read (Pull)
Build feed at read time by fetching posts from all followed users. No write amplification. But high read latency. Works well for low-follower accounts.',
