SELECT '129d6d4c-abd4-797b-a6dd-43d4b7034f39', 'e9e0339e-d23e-7751-ae43-aeac3afae8e2', 'Branching & Checkout', 'Branching & Checkout', 'Creating parallel lines of development to build features in isolation.
Branch
A Branch in Git is a lightweight, moveable pointer to a specific commit. By default, projects start with a default branch (typically main). Creating a new branch creates a separate pathway of history so you can build features or fix bugs without affecting the stable production code.
Branching Flow Chart
Commit 1 → Commit 2 (main) → Commit 3 (main)
Commit 2 (main) ↳ checkout new branch → Feature Commit A → Feature Commit B
Branching Commands
Command	Purpose	Description
git branch	List Branches	Lists all local branches in the repository.
git checkout [branch]	Navigate Branch	Switches the working directory to the target branch.
git checkout -b [new-branch]	Create & Navigate	Creates a new branch and switches to it in one step.
git branch -d [branch]	Delete Branch	Deletes a branch (requires that changes are merged).
Interview tip
On modern versions of Git, the checkout command can be replaced with git switch (e.g. git switch -c new-branch to create and switch), separating branch navigation from file restoration.',
  setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Branching & Checkout'), 'A')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Branching & Checkout'), 'B')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Creating parallel lines of development to build features in isolation.
Branch
A Branch in Git is a lightweight, moveable pointer to a specific commit. By default, projects start with a default branch (typically main). Creating a new branch creates a separate pathway of history so you can build features or fix bugs without affecting the stable production code.
Branching Flow Chart
Commit 1 → Commit 2 (main) → Commit 3 (main)
Commit 2 (main) ↳ checkout new branch → Feature Commit A → Feature Commit B
Branching Commands
Command	Purpose	Description
git branch	List Branches	Lists all local branches in the repository.
git checkout [branch]	Navigate Branch	Switches the working directory to the target branch.
git checkout -b [new-branch]	Create & Navigate	Creates a new branch and switches to it in one step.
git branch -d [branch]	Delete Branch	Deletes a branch (requires that changes are merged).
Interview tip
On modern versions of Git, the checkout command can be replaced with git switch (e.g. git switch -c new-branch to create and switch), separating branch navigation from file restoration.'), 'C'),
  TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
