SELECT '25b43d82-6a27-748c-9d04-e17930b58a6f', '6b5acacf-db12-7e5c-9708-b06e57d86299', 'Repository & Cloning', 'Repository & Cloning', 'Creating a local folder copy of remote GitHub repositories.
Repository (Repo)
A Repository is a database folder containing all your project files and their complete version history logs (the metadata is stored inside a hidden folder called .git).
Cloning a Remote Repository
To duplicate an existing remote repository hosted on GitHub down to your local machine, use the git clone command along with the HTTPS or SSH link:
git clone https://github.com/username/my-project.git
This command automatically does the following:
Creates a new folder matching the repository name.
Initializes a local Git database inside it.
Fetches all the history branches and commits.
Checks out the default branch (usually main or master).
Configures the remote source address as origin.
Basic Terminal Operations
Command	Purpose	Description
cd [dir]	Change Directory	Navigates into the specified folder.
ls	List Files	Lists all visible files in the directory.
ls -a	List All	Lists all files, including hidden files (like the .git folder).',
  setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Repository & Cloning'), 'A')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Repository & Cloning'), 'B')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Creating a local folder copy of remote GitHub repositories.
Repository (Repo)
A Repository is a database folder containing all your project files and their complete version history logs (the metadata is stored inside a hidden folder called .git).
Cloning a Remote Repository
To duplicate an existing remote repository hosted on GitHub down to your local machine, use the git clone command along with the HTTPS or SSH link:
git clone https://github.com/username/my-project.git
This command automatically does the following:
Creates a new folder matching the repository name.
Initializes a local Git database inside it.
Fetches all the history branches and commits.
Checks out the default branch (usually main or master).
Configures the remote source address as origin.
Basic Terminal Operations
Command	Purpose	Description
cd [dir]	Change Directory	Navigates into the specified folder.
ls	List Files	Lists all visible files in the directory.
ls -a	List All	Lists all files, including hidden files (like the .git folder).'), 'C'),
  TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-10-07 03:23:53+00'
