INSERT INTO "notes"."NoteSearchDocument" ("noteId", "versionId", "title", "topics", "body", "document", "updatedAt")
SELECT '2bde528f-6732-740d-974f-f763c2033eb3', '4de52879-b02c-7893-bbc1-da35fc274f12', 'Diffusion & GANs', 'Diffusion & GANs', 'Exploring architectures powering image, audio, and video generation.
Diffusion Models
Generates images by learning to denoise a starting image of pure random Gaussian noise. 
- Forward Process: Iteratively adds noise to a real image until it becomes pure noise (analytic, no training). 
- Reverse Process: A neural network (a U-Net, or in newer models a Diffusion Transformer (DiT)) is trained to predict the noise added at each step, allowing it to subtract noise iteratively to recover a clean, generated image.
Stable Diffusion · DALL·E · Latent Diffusion
GANs (Generative Adversarial Networks)
A game-theoretic framework with two neural networks competing: 
- Generator: Tries to create fake data (images) that look real. 
- Discriminator: Tries to distinguish between real images and fake images generated by the Generator. 
They train simultaneously in a minimax loop, driving the Generator to output highly realistic details.
StyleGAN · CycleGAN · Minimax Loss',
  setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Diffusion & GANs'), 'A')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Diffusion & GANs'), 'B')
    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Exploring architectures powering image, audio, and video generation.
Diffusion Models
Generates images by learning to denoise a starting image of pure random Gaussian noise. 
- Forward Process: Iteratively adds noise to a real image until it becomes pure noise (analytic, no training). 
- Reverse Process: A neural network (a U-Net, or in newer models a Diffusion Transformer (DiT)) is trained to predict the noise added at each step, allowing it to subtract noise iteratively to recover a clean, generated image.
Stable Diffusion · DALL·E · Latent Diffusion
GANs (Generative Adversarial Networks)
A game-theoretic framework with two neural networks competing: 
- Generator: Tries to create fake data (images) that look real. 
- Discriminator: Tries to distinguish between real images and fake images generated by the Generator. 
They train simultaneously in a minimax loop, driving the Generator to output highly realistic details.
StyleGAN · CycleGAN · Minimax Loss'), 'C'),
