). "},{"type":"text","text":"Labels","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are the ground-truth targets or outputs the model is trying to predict (e.g., house price)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loss Function","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A mathematical function that measures how far the model''s predictions are from the true labels. The goal of training is to minimize this loss. Examples: Mean Squared Error (MSE), Cross-Entropy."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Epoch vs Batch","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"text","text":"batch","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the subset of training samples passed through the network in one forward/backward pass. An "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" represents one complete pass of the entire training dataset."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gradient Descent","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"An optimization algorithm used to minimize the loss function by iteratively updating the model''s weights in the opposite direction of the gradient (steepest ascent) of the loss curve."}]}]}]}]}}')
